From 5ea7ac52602a854a433489a1aa57e323d55342f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:35:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] fix(api): echo X-Correlation-Id on every error and
 declare the header

The limit check on both list endpoints and the delete conflict path built
their error envelopes with a fresh random id, so a caller (or the gateway,
which always forwards X-Correlation-ID) could not match those errors to its
request, unlike every other error response.

A router-level get_correlation_id dependency now provides the id to the
routes that build envelopes themselves, and makes every endpoint declare the
header, which the OpenAPI contract now documents as a shared parameter on all
business paths.
